more likely to be fatal than in an older man with a history of coronary heart disease because","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the older man is less active and will not overtax his heart"},{"label":"B","text":"the young man has a better functioning coagulation mechanism"},{"label":"C","text":"the older man will probably have poorly functioning heart valves and will be unable to develop high intraventricular pressures"},{"label":"D","text":"the older man will have a well-developed collateral circulation in the coronary system"},{"label":"E","text":"the younger man will have less mature collagen in his heart wall"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-783995d1c146","stem":"Cerebral embolization occurring as a complication of a myocardial infarct would most probably be indicative of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"disseminated intravascular coagulation"},{"label":"B","text":"mural thrombus in the left ventricle"},{"label":"C","text":"lack of collateral circulation"},{"label":"D","text":"post-myocardial injury syndrome"},{"label":"E","text":"phlebothrombosis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationSta