ng a fully histocompatible stem cell donor for transplantation is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"~100%"},{"label":"B","text":"~50% C ~25%"},{"label":"D","text":"~10%"},{"label":"E","text":"~05% 6 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-6f67a7913875","stem":"The ideal management for a 34 year old Middle Eastern prince with relapsing diffuse large B- cell lymphoma presenting with generalized lymphadenopathy, marrow and blood infiltration is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Wait and watch policy"},{"label":"B","text":"Local radiation therapy"},{"label":"C","text":"Rituximab"},{"label":"D","text":"R-CHOP E Hematopoietic stem cell autotransplantation"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1670038183c2","stem":"The ideal management for a 54 year old patient presenting with diffuse large B- cell lymphoma extensively involving the mediastinum, both cervical lymph nodes, and the spleen is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Wait and watch policy"},{"label":"B","text":"Local radiation therapy"},{"label":"C","text":"Rituximab D R-CHOP followed by mediastinal irradiation"},{"label":"E","text":"Hematopoietic stem cell autotransplantation"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7f7a843b75fa","stem":"The ideal management for a 54 year old patient with stage IV diffuse large B- cell lymphoma presenting with generalized lymphadenopathy, marrow and blood infiltration is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Wait and watch policy"},{"label":"B","text":"Local radiation therapy"},{"label":"C","text":"Rituximab D R-CHOP"},{"label":"E","text":"Hematopoietic stem cell autotransplantation"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-dc75a3717d3c","stem":"A 40 year acute myeloid leukemia patient with hyperleukocytosis and poor karyotypic features failed to go to remission after two courses of induction. He partially responded to anti CD33 Mylotarg “Ozagamicin”. He has a monozygotic twin brother, two fully matched siblings and many family members who are one antigen mismatch. Patient was advised for peripheral stem cell transplantation. To give the best chance for cure in this patient, what type of stem cell transplantation you will chose?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Syngeneic transplantation from the monozygotic twin brother B Allogeneic transplantation from one of the fully-matched siblings"},{"label":"C","text":"Autotransplantation after high dose chemotherapy"},{"label":"D","text":"Cord blood transplantation"},{"label":"E","text":"No transplantation"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"3d8dfd78d440abc669e079bdb46faef204c2ff7d"},{"id":"q-61c11087d265","stem":"All but one of the followings is true in one antigen mismatched stem cell transplantation","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Survival is as good as fully matched transplants in acute myeloid leukemia"},{"label":"B","text":"There is more chance for GvHD “Graft versus Host Disease”"},{"label":"C","text":"It is associated with more Graft versus Tumor effect D Preferable to fully matched transplants in aplastic anemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Preferable to matched unrelated donors in chronic myeloid leukemia 7 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topi