{"label":"E","text":"CNS could be involved 13 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-755a6cd48721","stem":"One of the following features is not true in the FAB classification of Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"M1 is AML of the myeloblasts B M2 is AML of the lymphoblasts"},{"label":"C","text":"M3 is AML of the promyelocytes"},{"label":"D","text":"M5 is AML of the monoblasts"},{"label":"E","text":"M7 is AML of the megakaryoblasts"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c54270990a40","stem":"Marked splenomegaly could be seen in any of the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Thalassemia major"},{"label":"B","text":"Chronic myeloid leukemia C Immune thrombocytopenic purpura “ITP”"},{"label":"D","text":"Kala Azar"},{"label":"E","text":"Malarial splenomegaly or Tropical Splenomegaly Syndrome"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8426254865ae","stem":"Granulomatous Lymphadenitis could result from any of the following “specific” conditions EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Tuberculosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Toxoplasmosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Sarcoidosis D Cushing’s disease"},{"label":"E","text":"Crohn’s disease"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4e462e055edc","stem":"One of the following features is not true in Nodular Sclerosis Hodgkin’s disease","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lacunar type of Reed Sternberg cells"},{"label":"B","text":"Anterior mediastinal mass"},{"label":"C","text":"No male preponderance"},{"label":"D","text":"Alcohol intolerance E The commonest type in the Middle East"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c20d62fdfd69","stem":"One of the following conditions cannot cause marked splenomegaly","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Osteopetrosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Niemann Pick disease"},{"label":"C","text":"Gaucher’s disease"},{"label":"D","text":"Hydatid disease of the spleen E Celiac disease"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-084e116ad7da","stem":"One of the following features is not true in Burkitt’s Lymphoma","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is associated with Epstein Barr virus infection and malaria B It is common at very high altitudes"},{"label":"C","text":"It usually affects the jaw bones or the viscera"},{"label":"D","text":"It is one of the most aggressive tumors but responsive to chemotherapy"},{"label":"E","text":"It has a “Starry-sky” tissue appearance"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7e71c095eaed","stem":"Renal failure complicates myeloma because of any one of the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Nephrology","topicOriginal":"Nephrology","subtopic":"Renal","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Amyloidosis of the Kidney"},{"label":"B","text":"Nephrocalcinosis from hypercalcemia"},{"label":"C","text":"Light chain damage to the renal tubules D Extensive infiltration of the kidney by myeloma cells"},{"label":"E","text":"Pyelonephritis secondary to immune paresis & neutropenia 14 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Nephrology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-1c3cd0a8276b","stem":"One of the following features is not true in Waldenstrom’s macroglobulinemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"IgM Gammopathy"},{"label":"B","text":"Hyperviscosity"},{"label":"C","text":"Splenomegaly and lymphadenopathy"},{"label":"D","text":"Cryoglobulinemia E Large Osteolytic bone lesions"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1a1d6e812cdc","stem":"One of the following features cannot happen in Myelofibrosis: A Splenic atrophy","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Nucleated red cells and myelocytes in the blood smear"},{"label":"C","text":"Hemopoiesis in the liver and spleen"},{"label":"D","text":"Tear drop red blood cells"},{"label":"E","text":"Portal hypertension"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8c6f275b56e5","stem":"One of the following features cannot happen in Essential Thrombocythemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Splenic atrophy"},{"label":"B","text":"GIT bleeding"},{"label":"C","text":"Thrombosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Splenomegaly E Thrombocytopenia"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9c9bde07e916","stem":"One of the following features cannot happen in Polycythemia Rubra Vera","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hyperviscosity"},{"label":"B","text":"Hypermetabolism"},{"label":"C","text":"Hyperuricemia D Splenic atrophy"},{"label":"E","text":"Pruritis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-29016208457d","stem":"All of the following Non-Hodgkin’s Lymphomas are intermediate grades in the “old” Working Formulation EXCEPT: A Burkitt’s lymphoma","type":"Calculation","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Follicular Large Cell lymphoma"},{"label":"C","text":"Diffuse Large Cell Lymphoma"},{"label":"D","text":"Diffuse Small Cleaved Cell Lymphoma"},{"label":"E","text":"Diffuse Mixed Cell Lymphoma"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-71ff3d83baa8","stem":"APTT cannot be prolonged in one of the following conditions","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"von Willebrand’s Disease"},{"label":"B","text":"Hemophilia A"},{"label":"C","text":"Christmas Disease"},{"label":"D","text":"Hageman Factor (XII) Deficiency E Factor VII Deficiency"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-28e751aa919a","stem":"All of the following features are true in Acute Childhood ITP EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Marrow megakaryocytosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Giant platelets with high Mean Platelet Volume (MPV) C Low incidence of spontaneous remission"},{"label":"D","text":"Prolonged bleeding time"},{"label":"E","text":"Purpuric superficial muco-cutaneous type of bleeding 15 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-4e82ce5b4ba6","stem":"Acute childhood ITP is characterized by all of the following features EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is usually a self limiting disease"},{"label":"B","text":"MPV “Mean Platelet Volume” could be more than 10 fL (Normal 5-8 fL) C No or few megakaryocytes in the bone marrow"},{"label":"D","text":"Platelet count is usually very low"},{"label":"E","text":"Good response to intravenous immunoglobulin"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bf7e3dcfa3a6","stem":"Thrombocytosis can result from any of the following causes EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hodgkin's Disease"},{"label":"B","text":"Ulcerative colitis"},{"label":"C","text":"Splenectomy D Aplastic anemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Steroid administration"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d74a71ffdd9f","stem":"All of the following relate to DIC EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hypofibrinogenemia"},{"label":"B","text":"Prolonged PT, APTT and bleeding time"},{"label":"C","text":"Thrombocytopenia"},{"label":"D","text":"Increased D-Dimer & Fibrin(ogen) Degradation Products (FDP) E DIC means “Death Is Coming”"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1acb07b6c89a","stem":"One of the following is not true in Acute Hypergranular Promyelocytic Leukemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It results from proliferation of promyelocytes"},{"label":"B","text":"The leukemic cells could be dumb-bell shaped without granules"},{"label":"C","text":"The chromosome abnormality t(15q+;17q-) is characteristic"},{"label":"D","text":"Treatment with ATRA could be very effective E Characterized by lymphadenopathy, gum hypertrophy & skin infiltration"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0638027eca57","stem":"All of the following features relate to Chronic Granulocytic Leukemia EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Philadelphia chromosome is positive in the majority of cases"},{"label":"B","text":"The chronic stage usually lasts about four years"},{"label":"C","text":"Segmented neutrophils and myelocytes are increased D Neutrophil alkaline phosphatase is high"},{"label":"E","text":"Usually terminates in blast crisis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c3bb254b5209","stem":"One of the following features is not true in Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia: A It is basically the disease of elderly people","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"It could happen in young adults"},{"label":"C","text":"It is the best type of children’s leukemia with a cure rate of >60%"},{"label":"D","text":"It is due to proliferation of lymphoblasts"},{"label":"E","text":"It could present as CNS leukemia"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9f388a340518","stem":"One of the following features is true in Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia: A Usually affects elderly people","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"It is not uncommon in children"},{"label":"C","text":"It results from uncontrolled proliferation of immature lymphocytes"},{"label":"D","text":"All patients should be treated immediately"},{"label":"E","text":"Thrombocytosis carries a poor prognosis 16 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-bfc25b76f4e8","stem":"Thrombocytopenia in Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia could not result from","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bone marrow infiltration by leukemic cells"},{"label":"B","text":"Autoimmune antibodies to platelets"},{"label":"C","text":"Hypersplenism D Varicella zoster"},{"label":"E","text":"Chemotherapy used in the management of the CLL"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2a2c13398706","stem":"Type 2N “N = Normandy” von Willebrand disease is due to","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Quantitative deficiency of von Willebrand Factor “VWF”"},{"label":"B","text":"Deficiency of the high molecular weight VWF multimers"},{"label":"C","text":"Increased binding of VWF to platelets causing depletion of high molecular weight VWF and thrombocytopenia"},{"label":"D","text":"Decreased binding of VWF to platelets, but with normal VWF multimers E Decreased binding of VWF to FVIII causing low plasma Factor VIII:c"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated",