sitive in: A AML without differentiation (M1)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Acute Monoblastic Leukemia (M5)"},{"label":"C","text":"Acute megakaryoblastic Leukemia (M7)"},{"label":"D","text":"Acute lymphoblastic Leukemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Hairy Cell Leukemia"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-76b1ebfb17c3","stem":"One of the following features is not true in Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (M3)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It used to have a very poor prognosis because of DIC following treatment"},{"label":"B","text":"It is now one of the best types of AML because of treatment with ATRA"},{"label":"C","text":"Faggot Cells ( Promyelocytes with bundles of Auer Rods) could be seen"},{"label":"D","text":"Strongly positive Sudan Black stain E Very strong TdT positivity 21 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-b687297ab65c","stem":"Acute leukemia patients cannot present with","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fungal infection"},{"label":"B","text":"Bacterial Infection"},{"label":"C","text":"Viral Infection D Empty bone marrow"},{"label":"E","text":"Mediastinal widening"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-641cbbfa91d8","stem":"In Acute Leukemia the white blood cell count could be","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"High (100,000/uL)"},{"label":"B","text":"Very high (250 000/uL)"},{"label":"C","text":"Low (1000/uL)"},{"label":"D","text":"Normal (10,000/uL) E All of the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a1f406f5b0cb","stem":"All of the following are true for chronic myeloid leukemia treatment EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Imatinib mesylate (Glivec) is a new revolutionary oral treatment"},{"label":"B","text":"Interferon can benefit many patients but side effects are troublesome"},{"label":"C","text":"Hydroxyurea is still the most widely used treatment"},{"label":"D","text":"Busulphan is no more used because of its long-term complications E Old patients should be given the choice of stem cell or marrow transplant"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f1e69ab99434","stem":"Which one is not true for chronic lymphocytic leukemia treatment","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rai stage IV patients benefit from steroid before proper chemotherapy B All Rai stage I & II patients should be immediately treated"},{"label":"C","text":"Fludarabine, Chlorambucil, Vincristine & Prednisolone are effective"},{"label":"D","text":"Coomb’s positive hemolytic anemia patients better be given steroid first"},{"label":"E","text":"Acyclovir should be used liberally for zoster and herpes simplex"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-83a147f986df","stem":"The following are regarded as Chronic lymphoproliferative disorders EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hairy cell leukemia"},{"label":"B","text":"Small lymphocytic lymphoma"},{"label":"C","text":"Waldenstrom’s macroglobulinemia D Burkitt lymphoma"},{"label":"E","text":"Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a95e4840238c","stem":"All of the following features relate to Hairy Cell Leukemia EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Splenomegaly B Granulocytosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Dry bone marrow aspiration tap"},{"label":"D","text":"Tartarate Resistant Acid Phosphatase (TRAP) positive cells"},{"label":"E","text":"Monocytopenia"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b9aba8815d89","stem":"All of the following features are true in Aplastic Anemia management EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Marrow or stem cell transplantation should be offered to all young patients"},{"label":"B","text":"Anti-lymphocyte Globulin could benefit many patients"},{"label":"C","text":"Chemotherapy could be effective in patients with marrow lymphocytosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Blood transfusion from potential marrow donors should be avoided E Supportive management with red cells, platelets & antibiotics has no role 22 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-f55c1dfef15c","stem":"All of the following are true for Vitamin B12 EXCEPT: A Mainly absorbed in the duodenum","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Nutrition and Dietetics","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"The daily requirement is 1 microgram"},{"label":"C","text":"The body stores are enough for many years"},{"label":"D","text":"Deficiency causes megaloblastic anemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Mostly available in meat products"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Nutrition and Dietetics","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a97f670b49d2","stem":"All but one of the following features are true about Cord Blood Stem Cell transplantation","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Histocompatibility mismatch is better tolerated B High numbers of stem cells is guaranteed"},{"label":"C","text":"The median time to availability is short since all supply are typed"},{"label":"D","text":"Associated with a lower incidence of GvHD"},{"label":"E","text":"Associated with a higher incidence of graft failure and slow engraftment"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7be42f6659ec","stem":"One of the following features is not true in Cord Blood Stem Cell transplantation","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"A poor source of future Donor Lymphocyte Infusion supply"},{"label":"B","text":"The cord stem cells could be from a baby with a genetic disorder"},{"label":"C","text":"Could be the only source in communities with diverse background D Engraftment is quick and steady"},{"label":"E","text":"Low incidence of GvHD"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-292627617f3f","stem":"All but one of the following statements is true about autologous transplantation","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Currently it is the commonest practiced form of stem cell transplantation B It could be associated with a modest degree of GvHD"},{"label":"C","text":"It does not have Graft versus Tumor effect"},{"label":"D","text":"The biggest drawback is the potential possibility of tumor contamination"},{"label":"E","text":"It seems to be the treatment of choice for multiple myeloma"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9a970eee6370","stem":"Finding a histocompatible matched unrelated donor “MUD” for a leukemia patient who needs stem cell transplantation is more difficult in","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Irish Americans B African Americans"},{"label":"C","text":"Japanese"},{"label":"D","text":"Nordic countries"},{"label":"E","text":"Korea"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-763ec6a2d582","stem":"The most probable form of stem cell transplantation for a Kurdish patient with Philadelphia negative chronic myeloid leukemia who had immigrated to Sweden and offered the procedure is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Matched Unrelated Donor transplantation"},{"label":"B","text":"Autotransplantation"},{"label":"C","text":"Syngeneic transplantation"},{"label":"D","text":"Allogeneic transplantation E Cord blood transplantation 23 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-477dac3f1ac4","stem":"The most probable form of stem cell transplantation for a Swedish patient with Philadelphia negative chronic myeloid leukemia, who is the only child in the family is: A Matched Unrelated Donor transplantation","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Autotransplantation"},{"label":"C","text":"Syngeneic transplantation"},{"label":"D","text":"Allogeneic transplantation E Cord blood transplantation"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b212018bc47c","stem":"The most frequent form of stem cell transplantation for patients with multiple myeloma is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Matched Unrelated Donor transplantation B Autotransplantation"},{"label":"C","text":"Syngeneic transplantation"},{"label":"D","text":"Allogeneic transplantation"},{"label":"E","text":"Cord blood transplantation"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ea3e26cdcf04","stem":"The best form of stem cell transplantation for a patient with aplastic anemia is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Matched Unrelated Donor transplantation"},{"label":"B","text":"Autotransplantation C Syngeneic transplantation"},{"label":"D","text":"Allogeneic transplantation"},{"label":"E","text":"Cord blood transplantation"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b78cde7f5ed8","stem":"The transplant of choice for a patient with thalassemia major is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Matched Unrelated Donor transplantation"},{"label":"B","text":"Autotransplantation"},{"label":"C","text":"Syngeneic transplantation D Allogeneic transplantation"},{"label":"E","text":"Cord blood transplantation"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6154a356b0bf","stem":"There is no role for hematopoietic stem cell transplantation in the initial treatment strategy of one of the following blood diseases: A Acute promyelocytic leukemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Acute myeloid leukemias"},{"label":"C","text":"Chronic myeloid leukemia"},{"label":"D","text":"Aplastic anemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Thalassemia major"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ea1de6ac2d67","stem":"Pronormoblasts are cells with all of the following features EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are the earliest recognizable erythroid cells"},{"label":"B","text":"They have deep blue basophilic cytoplasm C They do not contain nucleoli"},{"label":"D","text":"They eventually give rise to normoblasts"},{"label":"E","text":"Their nuclei are round and consist of finely stippled chromatin"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-acace1a0563f","stem":"Promyelocytes are cells with all of the following features EXCEPT: A They are the earliest granulocyte precursors","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Their nuclei contain few nucleoli"},{"label":"C","text":"Their cytoplasm contain granules"},{"label":"D","text":"They will give rise to myelocytes"},{"label":"E","text":"They may be larger than myeloblasts 24 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-9f4f460ea67d","stem":"Plasma cells have all of the following features EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are the end stage cells in the lymphoid lineage"},{"label":"B","text":"They produce immunoglobulins"},{"label":"C","text":"They are elliptical fried-egg like cells with eccentric nuclei"},{"label":"D","text":"Their nuclear chromatin is coarse and clumped E They can normally be seen in the peripheral blood smear"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b329ebfcb3ad","stem":"Megakaryocytes are characterized by all of the following EXCEPT: A They are the largest cells in the peripheral blood smear","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"They produce platelets"},{"label":"C","text":"They are usually multinucleated"},{"label":"D","text":"Their cytoplasm is full of azurophilic granules"},{"label":"E","text":"They can reach the size of up to 100 micrometer in diameter"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d5553ee96497","stem":"The following features relate to the red cell anomalies","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Anisocytosis indicates difference in shape"},{"label":"B","text":"Poikilocytosis indicates difference in size"},{"label":"C","text":"Howell-Jolly bodies are precipitated denatured hemoglobin"},{"label":"D","text":"Heinz bodies are nuclear remnants E Polychromasia usually indicates reticulocytosis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-37f0eda23b0d","stem":"All of the following hematological values are normal EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"A hemoglobin of 10 gm/dL in a three month old child"},{"label":"B","text":"A hematocrit of 60% in a newborn"},{"label":"C","text":"An MCV of 100 femtoliter in a newborn D Red cell volume of 38 ml/Kg body weight in an adult male"},{"label":"E","text":"A neutrophil count of 2000/uL in a Saudi medical student"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2eb735c7047c","stem":"The followings relate to Glucose-6-Phosphate Dehydrogenase Deficiency","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Usually affects female patients"},{"label":"B","text":"G6PDH is important in the Embden-Meyerhof (Glycolysis) cycle to provide reducing power for the protection of the red cells from oxidative injuries"},{"label":"C","text":"Favism usually happens three days after eating beans D Inheritance of the deficient gene is sex-linked"},{"label":"E","text":"Acute Drug-induced hemolysis happens immediately after taking the drug"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7ce0818ee2e5","stem":"One of the following features is not true in pernicious anemia: A It is due Vitamin B12 deficiency from poor intake","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"It is due to autoantibodies against the gastric parietal cells"},{"label":"C","text":"Marrow erythropoiesis is active but ineffective"},{"label":"D","text":"Blood smear shows oval macrocytes and hypersegmented neutrophils"},{"label":"E","text":"There is severe lack of intrinsic factor"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b5e0c038f4b6","stem":"One of the following features is correct in hereditary spherocytosis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is autosomal recessive"},{"label":"B","text":"Usually associated with marked unconjugated hyperbilirubinemia"},{"label":"C","text":"Usually associated with marked conjugated hyperbilirubinemia"},{"label":"D","text":"Splenectomy reverses the red cell shape to biconcave form E Severe unexpected anemia could result from Parvovirus B19 infection 25 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-a6ddb8ea2b83","stem":"One of the following features is not true in Warm Autoimmune Hemolytic Anemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is usually due to IgG antibodies B It is usually due to IgM antibodies"},{"label":"C","text":"Steroid therapy &/or splenectomy usually benefit the patient"},{"label":"D","text":"The spleen is often enlarged"},{"label":"E","text":"Coomb's test is usually positive"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-fd10280c0857","stem":"The following statements relate to Sickle Cell Trait","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Patients usually present with painful crises"},{"label":"B","text":"Hemoglobin S is usually more than 50% C They are usually protected from Plasmodium falciparum infection"},{"label":"D","text":"Patients are usually symptomatic from their anemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Priapism is common"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-23e200ab4a73","stem":"One of the following features relate to β- thalassemia major : A Splenomegaly","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Splenic atrophy from repeated vaso-occlusion"},{"label":"C","text":"High hemoglobin F at around 40%"},{"label":"D","text":"Reduced iron absorption"},{"label":"E","text":"Effective erythropoiesis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5aad71eb4515","stem":"All of the following features relate to hemophilia A EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prolonged APTT B Prolonged bleeding time"},{"label":"C","text":"It is usually a male disease"},{"label":"D","text":"It is transmitted by female"},{"label":"E","text":"Joint and deep-seated bleeding is common"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-40af11bd63af","stem":"von Willebrand disease is characterized by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prolonged prothrombin time"},{"label":"B","text":"Deficiency of the coagulant portion of factor VIII (VIII:c) C Prolonged bleeding time"},{"label":"D","text":"It only affects male"},{"label":"E","text":"Hemarthrosis is common"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b2a2363d7441","stem":"Thrombocytopenic Purpura could complicate any of the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Acute Leukemia"},{"label":"B","text":"Aplastic anemia C Pure red cell aplasia"},{"label":"D","text":"Myelodysplastic syndromes"},{"label":"E","text":"Bone marrow metastasis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-585deec9ef49","stem":"Thrombocytosis can result from any of the following conditions EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Severe iron deficiency from a chronically bleeding duodenal ulcer"},{"label":"B","text":"5 q- Syndrome"},{"label":"C","text":"Splenectomy D Aplastic anemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Steroid administration 26 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-e8be4366fae2","stem":"All of the following are true in DIC EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It could complicate snake bite"},{"label":"B","text":"It could complicate mismatched blood transfusion"},{"label":"C","text":"Prolonged PT, APTT and bleeding time"},{"label":"D","text":"It is quite common in obstetric practice E Should never be treated with platelet & FFP because fuel is added to the fire"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b55e9cd60ee1","stem":"One of the following cannot happen in Chronic Granulocytic Leukaemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Priapism"},{"label":"B","text":"Gout"},{"label":"C","text":"Weight loss from hypermetabolism"},{"label":"D","text":"Acute abdomen from splenic infarction E Thrombocytopenia unless in blast crisis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ad88bb01e180","stem":"Only one of the following features is true in Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is basically the disease of elderly people"},{"label":"B","text":"White cell count is always high in the blood"},{"label":"C","text":"Bone marrow or stem cell transplantation is the early treatment of choice"},{"label":"D","text":"Only a minority of patients could be cured of their disease E It could present as CNS leukemia, which has a worse prognosis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-917a249abd44","stem":"All of the following is true in Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia EXCEPT: A All stages of the disease should be treated immediately","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Fludarabine and Chlorambucil are known drugs in the treatment of CLL"},{"label":"C","text":"Rai and Binet staging systems are utilized in grading the stage of CLL"},{"label":"D","text":"Could be confused with small lymphocytic lymphoma"},{"label":"E","text":"Bone marrow or stem cell transplantation do not benefit majority of patients EACH OF THE FOLLOWING MULTIPLE CHOICE QUESTIONS IS COMPOSED OF A STEM AND FIVE STATEMENTS. EACH OF THE STATEMENTS COULD BE TRUE OR FALSE. IN YOUR ANSWER SHEET, YOU ARE REQUESTED TO FILL THE CORRECT ONES AND LEAVE THE FALSE ONES EMPTY."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-66bd6138a66a","stem":"The following statements concern normal hematological values : A The normal MCV is between 76 and 96 milliliters","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"A hemoglobin of 10 gm/dL is normal for a three month old child"},{"label":"C","text":"A 70 Kg adult male has around ten units of whole blood D The red cell life span is between two and three months"},{"label":"E","text":"The red cell count of a full term infant is less than an adult male 27 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-21dca3ff0280","stem":"The following statements relate to iron status in the human body : A The normal amount of iron in an adult male is about 15 gms","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"The bone marrow needs about 30 mg of iron daily to produce red cells"},{"label":"C","text":"A menstruating female requires about three milligrams of iron daily D Excessive TEA consumption increases iron absorption E Unconjugated iron binding capacity is reduced in iron deficiency anemia"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a283eeb66d32","stem":"Macrocytosis could happen in any of the following conditions","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Alcoholic liver cirrhosis B Thalassemia"},{"label":"C","text":"Newborn D Iron overload"},{"label":"E","text":"Folic acid deficiency"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-613ed4a7e5d5","stem":"The following statements relate to Sickle Cell Anemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is common in the Asir region of Saudi Arabia B It only affects male patients"},{"label":"C","text":"Sickle cell trait protects against Falciparum malaria D It results from reduced production of β-globin chains E Patients with low hemoglobin should immediately be transfused"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-81fc9ba90718","stem":"The following features relate to Sickle Cell Disease","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Splenomegaly at early childhood B Hemoglobin S of 40%"},{"label":"C","text":"Leg ulcers"},{"label":"D","text":"Hand-foot syndrome E Symptomatic anemia"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-25c5d83c4e31","stem":"Sicklers can present with any of the following features","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Biliary colic"},{"label":"B","text":"Priapism C Marked splenomegaly immediately after birth"},{"label":"D","text":"Salmonella osteomyelitis E Splenic atrophy in the neonatal period"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bda9ccdf7f20","stem":"The following features relate to Sickle Cell Trait: A Severe hypochromic microcytic anemia B Extramedullary hemopoiesis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"C","text":"Splenic syndrome at high altitude"},{"label":"D","text":"Sickling problems during long flights in unpressurized aircrafts E Hemoglobin S of 73% Q179 The following statements relate to thalassemias:"},{"label":"A","text":"Patients with low hemoglobin should be transfused B β-thalassemia is due to replacement of Glutamic acid by Valine C High Hemoglobin F in a neonate indicates β- thalassemia major"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemoglobin electrophoresis is essential for proper diagnosis E Hemoglobin F has a low affinity for oxygen 28 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-098c5abff2a1","stem":"The following statements relate to β- thalassemia minor : A Normal hemoglobin A2","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Hypochromic microcytic red cells"},{"label":"C","text":"Increased numbers of red cells D Severe anemia necessitating transfusions"},{"label":"E","text":"Should be counseled regarding marriage to another β- thalassemia minor"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-10a42800bcbe","stem":"The following features are seen in β- thalassemia intermedia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Iron overload B Continuous and persistent need for blood transfusion"},{"label":"C","text":"Paravertebral extramedullary hemopoietic deposits"},{"label":"D","text":"Deafness from temporal bone involvement E Positive Coomb’s test"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6881e6ebe4bb","stem":"The following laboratory results relate to β- thalassemia major","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Labor and Delivery","options":[{"label":"A","text":"High Hemoglobin F"},{"label":"B","text":"Mild unconjugated hyperbilirubinemia C Normal hemoglobin A"},{"label":"D","text":"Hypochromic microcytic red cells with many target & nucleated red cells E sickle shaped red cells"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f0624682fbff","stem":"The following statements relate to Acute Monoblastic leukaemia (M5) : A It has the best prognosis between the subtypes of AML","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Non-specific Butyrate Esterase is positive in the leukemic monoblasts C DIC is very common if patients are not heparinized before treatment"},{"label":"D","text":"Gum hypertrophy, skin involvement and lymphadenopathy are common"},{"label":"E","text":"Lysozyme enzyme is usually elevated"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2c88832ed725","stem":"The following tests relate to hemostatic tests : A Prolonged prothrombin time is usually due to prothrombin deficiency","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Prolonged APTT could be due to Factor VIII:c deficiency"},{"label":"C","text":"Severe hypofibrinogenemia could result in prolonged PT, APTT & TT"},{"label":"D","text":"Factor X deficiency results in prolonged PT & APTT but not TT E Bleeding time is prolonged in Hemophilia A"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-75ebaf7f2734","stem":"The following statements are true about von Willebrand Disease","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prolonged bleeding time"},{"label":"B","text":"Failure of platelet aggregation to Ristocetin"},{"label":"C","text":"Menorrhagia"},{"label":"D","text":"APTT could be normal E Sex-linked inheritance"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-afa3fd0fa006","stem":"Thrombin Time (TT) is prolonged in the following situations","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Patients on Heparin therapy B Prothrombin deficiency C von Willebrand Disease"},{"label":"D","text":"Severe hypofibrinogenemia E Hemorrhagic Disease of the Newborn"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2124224bb583","stem":"The following statements relate to Glucose-6-Phosphate Dehydrogenase","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"200 million people are deficient of this enzyme worldwide B Deficiency can cause severe extravascular hemolysis C Splenomegaly is a particular feature of Favism"},{"label":"D","text":"Deficiency is believed to protect against malaria"},{"label":"E","text":"Hemoglobinemia, hemoglobinuria & hemosiderinuria can occur"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-51c6de8fa972","stem":"In Cold Hemagglutinin Disease (CHAD)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Coomb's test could be positive B Splenomegaly is usually marked"},{"label":"C","text":"Could be due to lymphoma"},{"label":"D","text":"MCV might be very high"},{"label":"E","text":"Blood samples should be taken into pre-warmed syringes and tubes"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ba13a99b40f7","stem":"The following statements relate to Paroxysmal Nocturnal Hemoglobinuria : A Autosomal recessive B Positive Coomb’s test","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"C","text":"Extreme sensitivity of the red cell membrane to complement lysis D Fragmentation anemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Budd Chiari syndrome (Hepatic vein thrombosis)"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-25fe46e1d2e9","stem":"Intravascular hemolysis could happen in the following diseases","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"CHAD “Cold Hemagglutinin Disease”"},{"label":"B","text":"PNH “Paroxysmal Nocturnal Hemoglobinuria”"},{"label":"C","text":"March Hemoglobinuria"},{"label":"D","text":"Mismatched ABO-incompatible blood transfusion"},{"label":"E","text":"G-6-P Dehydrogenase deficiency"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-fc252c6c5b07","stem":"Fragmentation anemia could complicate the following conditions","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prosthetic cardiac valve"},{"label":"B","text":"Burn"},{"label":"C","text":"Hemolytic Uremic Syndrome (HUS)"},{"label":"D","text":"Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura (TTP)"},{"label":"E","text":"March hemoglobinuria 30 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ Select the most appropriate answer:"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-11c52b8dc1fe","stem":"One of the following features is not true about Hereditary Elliptocytosis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is an autosomal dominant disease"},{"label":"B","text":"Usually associated with mild splenomegaly"},{"label":"C","text":"Reticulocytosis is a common feature"},{"label":"D","text":"Usually results from structural membrane protein defects E HbF could be high"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-71c3661a99a1","stem":"Splenomegaly is not a prominent feature of one of the following hemolytic anemias","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hereditary spherocytosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Sickle cell disease in early childhood"},{"label":"C","text":"Thalassemia major in adolescents D Paroxysmal Nocturnal Hemoglobinuria"},{"label":"E","text":"Osteopetrosis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b14324224bd2","stem":"One of the following is not true in the W.H.O. Mantle Cell Lymphoma","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Described as Centrocytic lymphoma in the Kiel classification B It has been found that these cells definitely come from the germinal centers"},{"label":"C","text":"The lymphoma cells are small to medium sized with cleaved nuclei"},{"label":"D","text":"Lymphomatous polyposis is a GIT form of Mantle cell lymphoma"},{"label":"E","text":"This type of lymphoma is usually nodular"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e6f3d12ba48c","stem":"All of the following cell markers are true in Mantle cell lymphoma EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"CD5 is commonly present"},{"label":"B","text":"Pan B cell markers (CD19, CD20, CD22 & CD79a) are positive"},{"label":"C","text":"CD 23 is lacking"},{"label":"D","text":"Cyclin D1 expression is common and diagnostically valuable E TdT is usually positive"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e75857720e0e","stem":"All of the following feature are true in Mantle cell lymphoma EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"t(11;14) is a characteristic cytogenetic abnormality B Blood and marrow spread is rare"},{"label":"C","text":"Prognosis and long term survival is poor"},{"label":"D","text":"Contrary to old belief, cells do not come from the germinal centers"},{"label":"E","text":"The growth pattern is commonly nodular or mantle zone pattern"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c1902d68774e","stem":"All of the following features are related to Infectious Mononucleosis EXCEPT: A Results from infection with Cytomegalovirus (CMV)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Positive Monospot test"},{"label":"C","text":"Atypical lymphocytosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Possible splenic rupture"},{"label":"E","text":"Development of antibodies to Epstein Barr virus (EBV)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a5173e481e83","stem":"One of the quantitative blood cell changes is not seen in Hodgkin lymphoma","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Eosinophilia B Basophilia"},{"label":"C","text":"Lymphopenia"},{"label":"D","text":"Thrombocytosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Anemia 31 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ Match the following types of leukemias with their morphological, cytochemical, immunological and clinical features. Each choice is used once only. (201). Pre-B Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia ......... (202). Acute Hypergranular Promyelocytic Leukemia (M3) ......... (203). Chronic Myeloid Leukemia ......... (204). Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia without Differentiation ......... (205). T- Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia ......... (A). A leukemic patient bleeding from Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation. Leukemic Promyelocytes with bundles of Auer rods forming “Faggot” cells seen. There is translocation between chromosomes 15 and 17. (B). A Middle aged patient with a very high white cell count without blasts. BCR-ABL fusion gene detected . Spleen is very big. (C). A child with a very high white cell count, most of which are blasts. Blasts are positive for acid phosphatase. Chest x-ray showed mediastinal widening. Immunological studies revealed blasts positive for CD5, CD7 and T- antigen. (D). A young patient with leukemia and 90% blasts. Blasts are positive for Sudan Black, Myeloperoxidase and Specific Esterase. No differentiation to promyelocytes seen. (E). A five year old child with anemia, neutropenia and thrombocytopenia. Bone marrow is full of blasts that are positive for CD 10, Cyt.u and TdT. Child responded nicely to chemotherapy and got cured of his disease. SELECT THE MOST APPROPRIATE SINGLE ANSWERS:"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["long_option_manual_review"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-d392c1dc2c82","stem":"Pan B cell markers (CD19, 20, 22 & 79a) are positive in all but one of these: A Sezary syndrome","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Follicular center cell lymphoma"},{"label":"C","text":"B- cell small lymphocytic lymphoma"},{"label":"D","text":"Hairy cell leukemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Diffuse large B- cell lymphoma"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c7a97c37935a","stem":"All of the following features are related to \"HYPERSPLENISM\" EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Splenomegaly"},{"label":"B","text":"Anemia"},{"label":"C","text":"Active bone marrow D Thrombocytosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Neutropenia"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not