swer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Results from proliferation of Myeloblasts"},{"label":"B","text":"Mature and maturing white blood cells are increased"},{"label":"C","text":"It is the commonest cancer in children."},{"label":"D","text":"Blasts are positive for Sudan Black"},{"label":"E","text":"Never cured by chemotherapy alone"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b13083edc1f8","stem":"Neutropenia could be seen in all of the following diseases EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Agranulocytosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Hepatitis"},{"label":"C","text":"Chronic Myeloid Leukaemia (CML) ."},{"label":"D","text":"Influenza"},{"label":"E","text":"Severe megaloblastic anemia"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-dfc5d7e2c2f3","stem":"Paraproteins could be seen in all of the following neoplasms EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Monoclonal Gammopathy of Undetermined significance"},{"label":"B","text":"Waldenstrom's Macroglobulinemia"},{"label":"C","text":"IPSID “Immunoproliferative Small Intestinal Disease”"},{"label":"D","text":"Chronic Lymphocytic Leukaemia (CLL)"},{"label":"E","text":"Burkitt lymphoma."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d5022e7870c5","stem":"Burkitt Lymphoma could present itself with all, but one, of the following features","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pautrier's abscess formation."},{"label":"B","text":"Intestinal obstruction in a child"},{"label":"C","text":"Tumor necrolysis syndrome after treatment"},{"label":"D","text":"Extreme sensitivity to Cyclophosphamide"},{"label":"E","text":"Aggressive nature"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7ebc38efcaa7","stem":"The following relates \"HYPOSPLENISM\"","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Splenomegaly"},{"label":"B","text":"Anemia"},{"label":"C","text":"Active bone marrow"},{"label":"D","text":"Target, pitted and Heinz-body containing red cells."},{"label":"E","text":"Neutropenia 44 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-082f4fd2aaac","stem":"You are provided with a table to comment on the hemostatic test results for some common bleeding disorders. Write “P” if you think the test is prolonged and “N” for a normal test result. To help you, many of the answers are already correctly labeled. The tests are: P.T. meaning Prothrombin Time","type":"True / False","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"P.T.T. meaning Activated Partial Thromboplastin Time"},{"label":"B","text":"T. meaning Bleeding Time T.T. meaning Thrombin Time The bleeding diseases are: vWD meaning von Willebrand’s Disease DIC meaning Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation ITP meaning Immune Thrombocytopenic Purpura Hemophilia which includes both Hemophilia A & B DISEASE OR FACTOR PT APTT TT B.T. DEFICIENCY HEMOPHILIA N vWD N N or P N XII & XI N N N VII N X, V & II N FIBRINOGEN P P N LIVER FAILURE P P N DIC ITP Select True (T) and False (F) answers."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"de08dc4592af7f86a6820ec35cba20209f94e45a"},{"id":"q-8958572ab31c","stem":"Myelofibrosis is often associated with","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Large spleen."},{"label":"B","text":"Lymphadenomegaly"},{"label":"C","text":"Philadelphia chromosome"},{"label":"D","text":"Gout."},{"label":"E","text":"Portal hypertension."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-eee8d7d57a33","stem":"The following are true of hemophiliacs","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Genes responsible for the disorder are carried on the Y chromosome"},{"label":"B","text":"The condition is inherited as sex-linked recessive characteristic."},{"label":"C","text":"Patients usually suffer from recurrent dislocation of joints"},{"label":"D","text":"Continued bleeding from the umbilical cord may be the earliest event."},{"label":"E","text":"Bleeding time is grossly prolonged 45 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-9cac2f2d8f5b","stem":"In Hemolytic Uremic Syndrome","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Purpura is a common feature."},{"label":"B","text":"It is much commoner in the USA than in the UK"},{"label":"C","text":"It appears suddenly in a previously healthy child."},{"label":"D","text":"It is associated with leucopenia"},{"label":"E","text":"Hemoglobinuria may occur."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c530d429131c","stem":"Sideroblastic anemia may be associated with","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Children with pulmonary Hemosiderosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Lead poisoning."},{"label":"C","text":"Myelodysplastic syndrome."},{"label":"D","text":"Partially treated hemorrhagic anemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Middle aged patient with a moderate refractory normoblastic anemia."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3858da2254cd","stem":"In Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fragmentation hemolytic anemia occurs."},{"label":"B","text":"Mainly males are affected"},{"label":"C","text":"Hypertension is usual"},{"label":"D","text":"Neurological manifestations are common."},{"label":"E","text":"There is a characteristic petechial rash."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2b5043b7fdff","stem":"Hemoglobinuria may occur in","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Incompatible blood transfusion."},{"label":"B","text":"Hereditary spherocytosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Hypersplenism"},{"label":"D","text":"Sickle cell anemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Drowning in fresh water."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0a40d240f471","stem":"Pernicious anemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Occurs with equal frequency at all decades over twenty"},{"label":"B","text":"May be associated with severe glossitis."},{"label":"C","text":"May present with mental disturbances."},{"label":"D","text":"The spleen is usually palpable"},{"label":"E","text":"Is usually associated with mild jaundice."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-704d8a4775cb","stem":"The following are part of the erythroid series","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pronormoblast."},{"label":"B","text":"Monoblast"},{"label":"C","text":"Plasma cell"},{"label":"D","text":"Megakaryocyte"},{"label":"E","text":"Promyelocyte"}],"prior