:"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"High LDH"},{"label":"C","text":"Hemoglobinuria"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemoglobinemia"},{"label":"E","text":"Hemosiderinuria"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bf093d6de7af","stem":"One of the following features does not relate to Wilson’s Syndrome: A It usually complicate alcoholism","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Serum Copper level is high"},{"label":"C","text":"There is reduced serum Caeruloplasmin"},{"label":"D","text":"Liver functions tests are usually abnormal"},{"label":"E","text":"There is toxic accumulation of copper in liver, red cells, cornea, kidney and brain 77 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-f0196f134e85","stem":"One of the following features is not true in Wilson’s Syndrome","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is an autosomal recessive disorder of copper metabolism"},{"label":"B","text":"It is also known as hepato-lenticular degeneration"},{"label":"C","text":"It could well be associated with hemolytic anemia"},{"label":"D","text":"Ophthalmoscopy shows Keyser-Fleischer rings E Coomb’s test is positive."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-619cb0396a1d","stem":"All but one of the following associations are true about Wilson’s syndrome","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Copper damage to liver could cause cirrhosis B Copper damage to red cells could cause Coomb’s positive hemolytic anemia"},{"label":"C","text":"Copper damage to kidney could cause Fanconi’s renal tubular acidosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Copper damage to brain could cause progressive neurological damage"},{"label":"E","text":"Copper damage to cornea could cause Keyser-Fleischer rings"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2fc04df20d95","stem":"In Wilson’s syndrome: A Hemolysis might antedate liver failure","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Ham’s test is usually positive"},{"label":"C","text":"Coomb’s test is usually positive"},{"label":"D","text":"Osmotic fragility is usually positive"},{"label":"E","text":"Sugar water test is usually positive"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8bc13188dbf0","stem":"The following immunizations are recommended prior to splenectomy for hemolytic anemias","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pneumovax"},{"label":"B","text":"Hib “Hemophilus influenza type b”"},{"label":"C","text":"Meningococcal vaccine D All of eth above"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-95955e12fd9f","stem":"In the new W.H.O. classification of Myelodysplastic syndromes “MDS”, All of the following are true about 5q- syndrome EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Usually affects female patients"},{"label":"B","text":"Platelet count could be high."},{"label":"C","text":"The anemia is usually macrocytic"},{"label":"D","text":"Dysmegakarypoiesis in the marrow E Prognosis is poor and survival is worse then other types of MDS"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f1b2eb63c9e6","stem":"All, but one of the following are true about ALIP “Abnormal Localization of Immature precursors”","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is an important feature of Myelodysplastic syndromes"},{"label":"B","text":"It is more frequent in RAEB “Refractory Anemia with Excess Blasts” C Pathognomonic for Myelodysplastic syndromes"},{"label":"D","text":"Usually inter-trabecular rather para-trabecular"},{"label":"E","text":"It is a marrow trephine biopsy feature"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c6bc02a8050d","stem":"All, but one, of the following support the diagnosis of Myelodysplastic syndromes: A Childhood onset","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Dyserythropoiesis"},{"label":"C","text":"Peripheral cytopenia"},{"label":"D","text":"ALIP “Abnormal Localization of Immature precursors” 78 Professor Anwar Sheikha, MD, FRCP, FRCPath., FACP One Thousand Hematology MCQ"},{"label":"E","text":"Hypercellular marrow"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-4d8b60f6c4cc","stem":"One of the following features is true in Myelodysplastic syndromes","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematol